  [acknowledged] disk/driver.asm:110: section header without inline citation: 'write path' (aa89e15851ff) — 'write path' — the write twin of the read path in the same file. Its body cites nothing itself because it mirrors dskio's read loop instruction for instruction ("Mirrors the read loop's structure exactly"), and the read path's own header block carries the PROVENANCE.md §FDC / §DSKIO interface citation that both rest on. A single shared citation for a mirrored pair is the honest shape; duplicating it would be prose written to satisfy a scanner. Human judgement, 2026-07-04, re-confirmed 2026-08-06.
  [acknowledged] disk/kernel.asm:557: section header without inline citation: 'MSX-DOS-1 kernel SETDTA-time entry: $5058 (M19)' (77d4c39b0be0) — 'MSX-DOS-1 kernel SETDTA-time entry: $5058 (M19)' — attested in full, in vocabulary CITATION does not carry: 12 comment lines naming the finding (M19), the probes (callseq / capture / callwatch causal pin), the black-box contract (entry register, write target, the register-identical 51-call comparison) and the clean-room line ("no stock routine internals decoded"). Widening CITATION with black-box was measured and DECLINED — docs/spec-audit-citations-review.md §2.5 records the numbers and the bar to re-open it. Kept as a review candidate deliberately: what counts as a citation is a judgement this tool declines to make.
  [acknowledged] disk/kernel.asm:8218: section header without inline citation: 'contract bodies (stubs; filled in milestone 4; added as each veneer lands)' (b7535589959f) — 'contract bodies (stubs; filled in milestone 4; added as each veneer lands)' — a table of bare `ret` stubs at pinned kernel addresses. It names no derived behaviour, so there is nothing to cite; each stub acquires its own citation in the comment block above it as the milestone that fills it lands (see the k_47B2 block immediately below, which cites tier2-m31-rdblk-randrecord-spec.md). Structural in substance but not in STRUCTURAL_HDR's vocabulary, and widening that regex to catch it would exempt far more than this one header.
